# Prettier ignores only node_modules / .git by default (it does NOT read
# .gitignore), so every build/generated/cache path prettier must skip is listed
# here explicitly. Keep in sync with .gitignore.

# Build output
**/lib
**/out
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test / coverage artefacts
**/coverage
**/unit-test-results
**/*test-results
**/playwright-report

# Turbo / Nx caches
.turbo
**/.turbo
.nx

# yalc (local package linking)
.yalc

# Generated code — Langium parser/AST + Theia browser-app scaffolding.
# `generated-transfer` is `hydranium-cli generate-transfer-model` output, kept
# out of `generated` because langium-cli treats its own output directory as
# exclusive and offers to delete anything else it finds there.
**/generated
**/generated-transfer
**/src-gen
**/syntaxes
examples/*/theia-app/plugins

# Throwaway probe scripts. A hand-written investigation left in the tree is not
# source and should not be able to redden `format:check`, which is the LAST
# clause of the chain and so reports after every other gate has already run.
*.tmp.mjs
*.tmp.ts

# Node diagnostic reports, written by --report-on-fatalerror into whichever
# directory the dying process was in. They appear only on a crash, so format
# noise here would land on top of the failure being investigated.
report.*.json
**/report.*.json

# Lockfile (npm-managed formatting)
package-lock.json

# Markdown — prettier's table-padding and emphasis normalization would churn
# prose-heavy planning/architecture docs on every edit for no correctness gain.
#
# So NO gate formats or checks markdown, and none is meant to: wrap, tables and
# emphasis are maintained by hand. `.editorconfig` is not that gate — it is
# advisory, applied by an editor and enforced by nothing here, and its markdown
# block only turns trailing-whitespace trimming OFF, because two trailing
# spaces are a hard line break. `check:readme` is the only check with teeth
# over markdown, and it typechecks fences rather than reading formatting.
#
# The format globs therefore do NOT name `md`. Adding it back reads as coverage
# and delivers none, since this rule wins.
**/*.md
